{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:537a8520d9acc818","name":"Flechette Mine","source":{"id":"source:reference-537a8520d9acc818","title":"Flechette Mine","revision":19445,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:59:16Z","sha256":"bd37a9094250dc2edd061a1b741b2aa0736f8b6d67fd8cda3c584afdacec9cfa","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19445","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Flechette%20Mine&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-537a8520d9acc818","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 1,200\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 0.5 Kilograms\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Availability:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Illegal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Illegal"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Mines, unlike traditional ",{"tag":"a","children":["Explosives"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Explosives"},", are designed to be placed in the ground or otherwise hidden from sight. Anyone attempting to notice a Mine takes a -5 penalty on his or her ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," check. Setting a Mine is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"}," that does not require a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check. However, attaching a detonator (either a Timer or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Manual Trigger"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Manual_Trigger","referenceId":"reference:3bac33a88449a688"},") requires a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check as usual, and supersedes the Mine's normal triggering system.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A Flechette Mine can cause grievous harm to anyone it damages. It contains thousands of tiny shards of metal that, when the Flechette Mine is triggered, fly into the air and bury themselves deeply into any targets within the blast radius. A Flechette Mine is placed on the ground (in any square adjacent to you) and is triggered when any character, creature, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"},", or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," enters the square in which it is placed. A Flechette Mine damages everything in a 2-Square ",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst"}," radius.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Size:"]}," Tiny\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 8d6 (Piercing)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Radius:"]}," 2-Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst"},")\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
